<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exserto</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exert-</span></b> ), āre, v. freq. a.
		exsero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To stretch out</i>, <i>thrust
			forth</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scyllam Ora exsertantem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 425</span></i>
			: linguam, Claud. Quadrig. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 9,
			13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacertos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 2, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurem per aulaeum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>listening eagerly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 14, 9, 3</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> (Acc. to exsero, I. B.) <i>To uncover</i>,
				<i>to bare</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humeros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 1, 412</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
